From 90acfa525403caa66588e6a9490783810efa01ff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan McClelland <rymcclel@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 16:51:06 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Forward Mobile: draw straight into the render target when
 the tonemap subpass would only be a copy

An LDR target with no adjustments, debanding or sky pass is drawn in one subpass
with the render target (or, under MSAA, its resolve) as the colour attachment:
no 10-bit scene buffer, no tonemap subpass, one attachment less in tile memory.
The scene shader applies the environment's tonemapper in its epilogue, with the
parameters carried in the scene UBO, and dithers itself when the viewport asked
for debanding. Off by default: rendering/renderer/mobile/render_directly_to_target.

The target is drawn through an sRGB view of its texture so the hardware encodes
and blending stays linear (rendering/renderer/mobile/direct_target_srgb_view);
without one the shader encodes. That view needed RenderingDevice to record the
override format on a shared texture: a framebuffer built on it declared the
owner's UNORM format and stored raw linear values on a Quest 3.

Measured on a Quest 3 arcade, MAX foveation, 545 MHz: MSAA 2x full view at
1.5x 5.6 -> 4.3 ms, empty frame at 1.75x 3.4 -> 3.1, non-MSAA full view at
1.5x 3.3 -> 3.7 (the per-fragment tonemap costs more than the subpass there).
