From 3b1d806a14ccacdc79bff662285df6a9e214bfbe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan McClelland <rymcclel@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 18:28:32 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Forward Mobile: the sky pass tonemaps on the direct
 render path

The direct pass refused any environment that draws a sky (or the fog-only sky
pass on a colour background) because the sky shader had no epilogue. The sky
UBO now carries the same tonemapper parameters and the direct flag; the main
sky pass tonemaps, and encodes when the target view is UNORM. The half and
quarter resolution passes stay linear, the main pass samples them.

Quest 3 arcade with a sky background, 1.5x, MAX foveation: 3.70 ms on the
subpass fallback, 3.59 on the direct pass, same picture.
---
 .../rendering/renderer_rd/environment/sky.cpp   | 12 ++++++++++++
 servers/rendering/renderer_rd/environment/sky.h |  7 +++++++
 .../forward_mobile/render_forward_mobile.cpp    | 17 ++++++-----------
 .../renderer_rd/shaders/environment/sky.glsl    | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 .../storage_rd/render_scene_data_rd.h           |  3 ++-
 5 files changed, 44 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

